+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-normalize-inventory-skus/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+## Context
+
+`Inventory` maps and movements use the SKU as given. `canonicalSku` in `src/catalog.ts` is the project's canonical form.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Import `canonicalSku` into `src/inventory.ts` and apply it at the top of each public method (`restock`, `reserve`, `release`, `ship`, `adjust`, `onHand`, `reserved`, `available`, `lowStock`, `movements`), so maps, movements, and error messages use the canonical SKU.
+- No new dependency or error type; quantities unaffected.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-normalize-inventory-skus/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-normalize-inventory-skus/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1e276d502fc953e22aba61b00a57cb48fad04b59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-normalize-inventory-skus/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+## Why
+
+`Catalog.find` normalises SKUs, but `Inventory` keys stock by the raw string. `restock('lb-220', 5)` adds stock under a different key from the `LB-220` that orders reserve, so the order fails as out of stock. The README says `ab-102`, ` AB-102 ` and `AB-102` are the same product.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `Inventory` canonicalises every SKU it receives (trim, upper case, via `canonicalSku`) in `onHand`, `reserved`, `available`, `restock`, `reserve`, `release`, `ship`, `adjust`, `lowStock` and `movements`.
+- Movements and low-stock rows show the canonical SKU.
+
+## Affected README rules
+
+Products: "SKUs are case-insensitive and ignore surrounding spaces". The code is brought in line; the README is unchanged.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+Anything other than SKU normalisation in `Inventory`; no catalogue, order, or error changes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `product-catalog`: the SKU rule also covers stock operations.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/inventory.ts`, `test/*.test.ts`.
